# Kavacha patch 0055 — search and palette follow-ups (REMAINING_WORK.md §3
# "Search & palette", closing all three items).
#
# 1. UNIVERSAL SEARCH SHORTCUT. Patch 0012 shipped universal search reachable
#    only through the command palette — press a shortcut, get a list, find
#    "Search Everything", press enter, then finally type. It has its own
#    command element and a rebindable binding now, listed in
#    about:preferences with every other shortcut. It ships UNBOUND on purpose:
#    every accel combination worth having is already taken by Firefox or Zen,
#    and silently stealing one from a user who upgrades is worse than making
#    them choose. This is a KBS versioner migration (19 -> 20), which is how
#    Zen adds shortcuts to existing profiles.
#
# 2. WORKSPACE FILTER TOGGLE. Patch 0012 put a workspaceId on every result it
#    could attribute and shipped the badge, leaving the filter as a follow-up.
#    The toggle is captured at OPEN, not per query, so switching Spaces
#    mid-search cannot silently change what "this Space" meant, and it resets
#    on close because scope is a per-search decision, not a setting — a sticky
#    filter would make the next search quietly miss things. Results with no
#    Space (bookmarks, downloads) are dropped rather than guessed at: inventing
#    an attribution would make the filter lie.
#
# 3. GROUPED PALETTE RENDERER. Patch 0027 stamped a `group` label on every
#    Kavacha command and nothing rendered it. Two things were missing, and the
#    non-obvious one is ordering: a header only means something if the rows of
#    its group are ADJACENT, and the results learner sorts by usage, which
#    interleaves domains freely. So the learner still ranks, but the
#    highest-ranked member of a domain decides where that whole domain sits and
#    the learner's order is kept within it. Rows with no domain — Zen's own
#    actions — keep their exact position; reordering upstream's results is not
#    this patch's business. The header is stamped onto the FIRST ROW of each
#    run rather than emitted as a result of its own, because a header row would
#    be selectable and would break arrow-key navigation. Clustering keys on the
#    domain, not the localized label: two domains could translate to the same
#    string, and deciding structure by comparing display text is how that class
#    of bug gets in.
#
# 4. PER-SPACE CONTEXT ENTRIES. Snapshot / branch / timeline existed only as
#    palette commands hard-wired to the ACTIVE Space, so there was no way to
#    act on a Space you could see but were not in. Branching a non-active Space
#    needs a snapshot of it first (kavachaBranchSpace's live path can only
#    snapshot the current window), which is what kavachaBranchSpaceFrom does.
#
# Why a patch: the shortcut needs a Zen command element, a zen-sets dispatch
# case and a KBS migration; the renderer is inside Zen's UrlbarProvider; the
# menu items live in Zen's popupset.
#
# Touches: src/browser/base/content/zen-commands.inc.xhtml, src/zen/common/zen-sets.js,
#          src/zen/kbs/ZenKeyboardShortcuts.mjs,
#          src/zen/kavacha-search/KavachaUniversalSearch.mjs + kavacha-search.css,
#          src/zen/urlbar/ZenUBGlobalActions.sys.mjs,
#          src/zen/urlbar/ZenUBActionsProvider.sys.mjs,
#          src/zen/common/styles/kavacha-spaces.inc.css,
#          src/browser/base/content/zen-panels/popups.inc,
#          src/zen/spaces/ZenSpaceManager.mjs,
#          locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-workspaces.ftl,
#          locales/en-US/browser/browser/preferences/zen-preferences.ftl.
# Applies on top of 0054.
